Subject: Cantor Public Procedure Machine Schema Derive Readiness

Description: Read-only assessment of the exact schemars capability boundary, stable naming, reachable derive blast radius, and serialization-direction issue after recursive representation formation.

@ [review_uuid] 2f357617-d83f-4bce-8438-33463bb193aa
@ [baseline_commit] bc547321c50d9429839bd3f769f0805a35d60df6
@ [schemars_version] 1.2.2
@ [schemars_checksum] 687274d293b6cdc6e73e0fee520bf2049650090d7164f87672d212a3c530cf4a

& [PinnedSourceFindings] are exact
  + SchemaSettings.draft2020_12 selects $defs and Draft 2020-12 explicitly
  + default contract is Deserialize and for_serialize selects Serialize
  + SchemaUid includes both type identity and contract
  + recursive insertion places a dummy definition before descending, preventing infinite derive expansion
  + schema_name supplies definition keys and collisions receive numeric suffixes based on use order
  + derive output shape is explicitly not semver stable and therefore requires canonical normalization and golden fixtures

& [BlastRadius] is 87 named types in 8 source files
  + 80 cantor_core types across model.rs 2, procedure.rs 60, procedure_authorship.rs 3, procedure_coordination.rs 2, procedure_tool.rs 11, procedure_verifier.rs 1, and temporal.rs 1
  + 7 cantor_procedure_tool transport wrappers in lib.rs
  + procedure.rs includes 17 closed enums emitted by one macro and 43 other reachable named definitions
  + no unrelated model, query, trust, temporal-runtime, service, MCP, ecosystem, or Windows type needs schema capability

& [CapabilityBoundary] should be optional and exact
  + workspace pins schemars exactly at 1.2.2 when a later activation permits Cargo mutation
  + cantor_core exposes an optional json-schema feature enabling the exact reachable types only
  + cantor_procedure_tool exposes an optional json-schema feature depending on cantor_core/json-schema
  + default builds do not compile or expose schema generation behavior
  + a later schema module enables the feature and owns generation, normalization, bounds, documents, and bundles

& [RemoteDerive] is rejected
  + schemars remote derive requires a structural copy and per-field with annotations
  + that duplicates 87 public contracts and creates a second review surface
  + compile-time checking does not remove semantic drift in serde attributes, bounds, or direction

& [StableNames] use verified unique Rust identifiers
  + the 80 core and 7 wrapper names are unique in the current closure
  + schema_name defaults to the declared Rust identifier and schema_id includes module path
  + canonical definition names use the expected inventory name and reject every collision suffix
  + an exact 87-name inventory test and golden definition-key set are mandatory
  + canonical document ids remain Cantor-owned URNs rather than schemars schema_id strings

& [ManualPrecision] is narrow
  + SemanticId requires schema annotations or a manual schema function for nonempty maximum-512 ASCII identity syntax
  + digest algorithm and value correspondence remains semantic because it is cross-field
  + core collection and semantic depth bounds remain residual when they depend on sibling ProcedureBounds

& [DirectionBlocker] prevents I02 activation
  + request documents describe deserialization acceptance
  + response documents describe serialization output
  + PreparedRunRequest is both prepare output and run input and may have direction-dependent definitions
  + one unqualified shared-definition map could silently reuse the wrong contract
  + define direction-qualified definition universes and fingerprints before activating derives

& [Disposition] is derive_boundary_selected_direction_profile_required
  + no code or Cargo mutation is authorized by this review

